  "implemented": [
    "Collapsed Review source interpretation panel explains uncertain classification, answers, stages, tools, unmapped content and extraction limits, with bounded original-source excerpts and honest page, sheet, row, line or extracted-block references.",
    "Review points focus existing editable controls without changing approval. Whole-document and worksheet evidence remain separate; source interpretation remains an advisory about the original extraction after manual editing.",
    "Recognizes explicit Sim/N\u00e3o and Pass/Fail answer labels, including printed N/A when present, accented Portuguese instruction/supervisor/declaration labels, and tool tables under explicit required-tools headings while retaining quantity and unit together.",
    "Strong Check/Inspection item headers outrank incidental Date/Time history when suggesting a checklist; genuine activity logs retain logbook classification. Unsupported response columns remain visible for manual review rather than copying historical answers.",
    "Toolbox imports offer an explicit Add instructions and tools to discussion action. It adds full retained source notes to the current edited outline, respects native prompt limits atomically and avoids duplicating identical existing source chunks.",
    "Import type changes and source-note copying enforce busy, uncertain-save, departed-form and capability guards in action code. Actual edits invalidate approval; inspection and identical no-op copying preserve it.",
    "Recognition evidence stays outside strict drafts and native save schemas. Existing inventory row selection, source coordinates, worksheet locations, SN/PN identities, Unknown quantities and all-or-nothing append protections remain included.",
    "Import help and asset/cache versions are updated through UI106. Existing artwork, account/mail/browser core, database schema, vendor parts and dependencies are preserved."
  ],
